  "evidence": "Obsidian's teams security help page says \"Obsidian does not support SSO.\" and that in most use cases Obsidian does not require an account or sign-on in the workplace; no SCIM or admin user management exists on any plan.",
  "notes": "New in 2026-09. Obsidian is a free local desktop/mobile app with no organisation admin console, SSO or SCIM. Paid services are per-user Obsidian Sync ($4/user/mo billed annually; shared vaults up to 20 collaborators, each needing their own Sync subscription, invited by the vault owner) and Publish ($8/site/mo billed annually). The optional Commercial license ($50/user/year) gives no in-app functionality and cannot be deployed by script. Sync is used as team_plan because it is the only paid tier that lets users work together. No user-management API exists (the Obsidian API is a plugin API).",
